<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Falvest yr shr plunges into red, div halved.</title>
<headline>Falvest yr shr plunges into red, div halved.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 1997</p>
<p>				   (million dollars)</p>
<p>    Shr, (U.S. cts)	 loss 29 vs 59 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			10 vs 20</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  loss 816 vs 1,636 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		loss 1,188 vs 3,153 profit</p>
<p>    Tax				79 vs 379</p>
<p>    Interest received	   441 vs 373</p>
<p>    Turnover		   25,388 vs 27,722</p>
<p>Full name: Falcon Investments Societe Anonyme</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said its revenue, which is derived from gold mining in Zimbabwe, fell to U.S.$25,39 million during the year from U.S.$27.72 million in the previous year, while costs rose 11 percent..</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
